# search_for(object, hint?): find an object. Simple version: rotate in place,
# run the detector on each frame, stop when the object is seen.
string object                          # detector class, e.g. "can", "ball"
string hint                            # optional, e.g. "behind the table"; "" = none (ignored this semester)
float32 timeout_s                      # 0 = default from config
---
bool success
string reason                          # "" on success; see docs/skills-contract.md
geometry_msgs/PointStamped location    # where the object is, odom frame. BT writes <object>.location
---
float32 rotated                        # rad turned so far
